# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
From: Odin Loch
Subject: [PATCH] gpu/cuda_hip: load and launch a caller's own modules

FORGE's CUDA/HIP runtime only runs its own embedded kernels. Add a minimal public API so a caller (here HGLN)
can load its own PTX / AMDGPU code object on the runtime's context and launch a kernel on the runtime's stream,
under the runtime's lock and context binding:

  load_module(image, &why) -> handle, module_function(m, name), unload_module(m)
  max_dynamic_smem(), set_dynamic_smem(fn, bytes)   (CUDA opt-in above 48 KB)
  launch_kernel(fn, grid[3], block[3], smem, args)  (through launch_s; wait() syncs)

Modules still loaded are unloaded in ~runtime before the context is destroyed. The device handle from init()
is kept (dev_) for the shared-memory attribute query. Against b135941680664502fec59924f51d3c3dc11e23e9.
Apply with `patch -p1` from the FORGE root.

diff -ru a/docs/gpu.md b/docs/gpu.md
--- a/docs/gpu.md
+++ b/docs/gpu.md
@@ -134,6 +134,7 @@
 | `argmax_resident(p, n)` | Greedy decode: `forge_argmax` over a device-newer buffer, one `int` read back into page-locked memory (ties: lowest index); `-1` when not resident. Up to 128 blocks scan the buffer and the last one to finish merges their partials (a 248k vocabulary: ~10 µs, against ~85 µs for one block). Wired as the `device_hooks::argmax` hook: with a plain greedy sampler, `session::generate` asks the executor for the logits' argmax instead of downloading them |
 | `capture_begin`, `capture_end`, `graph_launch` | User stream capture |
 | `copy_to_peer`, `device_alloc`, `device_free`, `upload`, `download` | Raw device memory and peer copies (host-staged when the APIs differ) |
+| `load_module(image, &why)`, `module_function(m, name)`, `unload_module(m)`, `max_dynamic_smem()`, `set_dynamic_smem(fn, bytes)`, `launch_kernel(fn, grid, block, smem, args)` | A caller's own kernels: load its PTX / code object on the runtime's context and launch on the runtime's stream (`wait()` or a download syncs). Modules are unloaded with the runtime |
 | `residency()`, `dispatches()`, `memory_pool()`, `charged_bytes()` | Statistics: uploads, downloads, resident and pooled bytes, evictions, per-kernel dispatch counts |
 | `cuda_hip::counters()` | Process-wide driver call counters (launches, captured, graph launches, copies, syncs) read by `forge bench` and `tools/bench_llm.sh` |
 
